  {
   "line_id": "S03",
   "title": "THE LINE",
   "headline": "THE LINE",
   "narration_text": "Every device has a reset line, a voltage it cannot go under, and I chose two volts. That gives the cell a limit, the biggest burst it can pass. Fresh, that is about a hundred milliamps. Remember this picture: the tank is the charge left, and the line is that limit.",
   "word_count": 51,
   "visual_intent": "A reset line at 2.0 V on the meter, 'my choice'. The chart returns with one point and a short stub at 100 mA, labelled 'about 100 mA, fresh' (the line itself is drawn in S04). A small legend holds for the rest of the Short: TANK = charge left, LINE = biggest burst the cell can pass.",
