  {
   "line_id": "S04",
   "title": "THE LINE MOVES",
   "headline": "THE LINE FALLS",
   "narration_text": "Now use the cell, and the resistor grows. Energizer's plot shows it going from ten ohms to about sixty-five. So the line comes down: a hundred milliamps at the start, about forty-three once nearly three quarters is spent, about eight and a half at the end. The tank empties slowly, but the line falls faster.",
   "word_count": 57,
   "visual_intent": "The line draws left to right and falls as the tank drains slowly: 100 mA at the start, about 43 mA at 150 mAh used (nearly three quarters), about 8.5 at the end. A small resistance strip, drawn by us: 10 ohm to about 65 ohm. Side by side, held 2 s or more.",
