  {
   "line_id": "S05",
   "title": "TWO ASKS",
   "headline": "SAME CELL, TWO ASKS",
   "narration_text": "Now let's make two asks. Eight milliamps never meets the line, so the device uses the whole cell. Sixty milliamps meets it with the tank still nearly half full, and the device resets with forty-eight percent left. The same cell, and the same tank. What changed is only how big a burst the device asked for.",
   "word_count": 57,
   "visual_intent": "An 8 mA ask line (labelled '8 mA') stays under THE LINE to the end: 'nothing left behind'. Then a 60 mA ask (labelled '60 mA') meets the line at about 108 mAh: RESET, the tank holds 48%. Both results shown together, held 2 s or more: '8 mA: 0% left behind' and '60 mA: 48% left behind (my model)'.",
